<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sealand Dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sealand Dynasty was a line of rulers in the marshy far south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> that broke away from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a>. According to the Babylonian Empire profile, it was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilum-ma-ili">Ilum-ma-ili</a> after defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samsu-iluna">Samsu-iluna</a>. Its independence deprived Babylon of southern revenues and halved the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sealand-dynasty.jpg" alt="Sealand Dynasty" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Gilgamesh_Dream_tablet._From_Iraq._Middle_Babylonian_Period,_First_Sealand_Dynasty,_1732-1460_BCE._Iraq_Museum,_Baghdad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
